rota lap 4562, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes (advanced by hand past row 2, which my last lap read). Its cardinal seat says run the census rather than read the sentence about it, so this lap ran tools/c/convergence_census.sh and let the reading choose the work.
think Cold roster opened at 09:46 and closed 235 green, 1 red, tree_moved=no. The red is standing_equipment reporting dated_path red, so reds came first.
think dated_path reads refs_lost=102 against a ceiling of 85. 97 of the 102 sit in dated testimony, which accrete-never-break forbids a lap to repair, and lost_promised_living reads 0. The scan already computes that split and its own header says moving the gate onto it waits on Keaton's word, asked on construction/ITINERARY.md -- and the card no longer carried the ask. Surfaced as a gate rather than routed around; the ask is back on the card.
think The one lawfully repairable member was in a living tool source: tools/c/convergence_tree_prove.sh named construction/archive/20260909-999999_itinerary-landed-accounts.md, a file written by a fault and removed the same hour. Rewritten to keep the fact without the path, under stamp-and-name's illustrate-with-placeholders clause. 103 -> 102.
think The census header named its own blindness on 20260909.185835 and left the repair a lap of its own: its population is picked by three shell idioms, so a Rishi tool could rewrite the tracked tree and never be a candidate. That is a page nobody answered, and it is this lane's work.
think Measuring moved the finding. The header pointed at write-file, Rishi's own write statement; across all 2,450 tracked .rish sources three tools call it with a literal target and git tracks none of the three. The real idiom is a redirect inside run ["sh" "-c" ...], and it has exactly one member -- tools/g/geode_libraries.rish, which tools/hooks/pre-commit runs on every commit and which the same header already calls proven-and-invisible.
think The fence is "sh" "-c" rather than the redirect: sh -c runs in this tool's own working directory, so its redirect is this tool's write, while a redirect handed to another tool as a flag value is text. Proven by mutation -- dropping the fence admits convergence_tree_prove_witness.rish on the --perturb string it runs against a worktree pen.
obs A leg that cannot fail proves nothing. The slash-rule leg read green with and without the rule, so it was retired to a plant that asserts nothing, and the rule was re-described as what it measurably is: a cost reading, 189s against 208s, changing no candidate, no member, and neither strand split.
obs The pen was green while the census died. A while loop carries its last body command's status, so rish_writes returned 1 whenever its final iteration emitted nothing, and set -e killed the run at rish=$(rish_writes "$f"). All nine new legs passed while that stood, because no plant bound a write-file target to an expression; the tree found it on the first source that did. That case is a plant and a leg now, and the leg bites.
